<italic toggle="yes">P</italic>
</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1" axis="1">Interaction <italic toggle="yes">P</italic>
</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Risk group</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="char" char="." rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.220</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="char" char="." rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.173</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;Low-risk</td><td align="char" char="." rowspan="1" colspan="1">570</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.872 (0.622&#x02013;1.222)</td><td align="char" char="." rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.425</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.249 (0.813&#x02013;1.919)</td><td align="char" char="." rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.309</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;Intermediate risk</td><td align="char" char="." rowspan="1" colspan="1">318</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.902 (0.650&#x02013;1.252)</td><td align="char" char="." rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.538</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.551 (0.334&#x02013;0.908)</td><td align="char" char="." rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.019</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;High-risk</td><td align="char" char="." rowspan="1" colspan="1">600</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.683 (0.546&#x02013;0.854)</td><td align="char" char="." rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x0003c;0.001</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.692 (0.521&#x02013;0.918)</td><td align="char" char="." rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x0003c;0.001</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Risk group integrate IA</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="char" char="." rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.062</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="char" char="." rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.112</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;Low-risk</td><td align="char" char="." rowspan="1" colspan="1">570</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.872 (0.622&#x02013;1.222)</td><td align="char" char="." rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.425</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.249 (0.813&#x02013;1.919)</td><td align="char" char="." rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.309</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;Subgroup1</td><td align="char" char="." rowspan="1" colspan="1">120</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.202 (0.696&#x02013;2.077)</td><td align="char" char="." rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.509</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.887 (0.388&#x02013;2.024)</td><td align="char" char="." rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.755</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;Subgroup2</td><td align="char" char="." rowspan="1" colspan="1">198</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.884 (0.579&#x02013;1.351)</td><td align="char" char="." rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.568</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.829 (0.476&#x02013;1.443)</td><td align="char" char="." rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.507</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;Subgroup3</td><td align="char" char="." rowspan="1" colspan="1">210</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.742 (0.495&#x02013;1.112)</td><td align="char" char="." rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.148</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.418 (0.224&#x02013;0.780)</td><td align="char" char="." rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.006</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;Subgroup4</td><td align="char" char="." rowspan="1" colspan="1">390</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.585 (0.450&#x02013;0.760)</td><td align="char" char="." rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x0003c;0.001</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.637 (0.460&#x02013;0.880)</td><td align="char" char="." rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.006</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">HIPC scheme</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="char" char="." rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.096</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="char" char="." rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.013</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;HIPC1</td><td align="char" char="." rowspan="1" colspan="1">570</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.872 (0.622&#x02013;1.222)</td><td align="char" char="." rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.425</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.249 (0.813&#x02013;1.919)</td><td align="char" char="." rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.309</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;HIPC2</td><td align="char" char="." rowspan="1" colspan="1">330</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.989 (0.704&#x02013;1.390)</td><td align="char" char="." rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.949</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.868 (0.547&#x02013;1.379)</td><td align="char" char="." rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.549</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;HIPC3</td><td align="char" char="." rowspan="1" colspan="1">588</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.636 (0.510&#x02013;0.793)</td><td align="char" char="." rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x0003c;0.001</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.580 (0.434&#x02013;0.775)</td><td align="char" char="." rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x0003c;0.001</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><fn fn-type="other"><p>HIPC, HCC imaging and pathological classification; HR, hazard ratio; OS, overall survival; RFS, recurrence-free survival.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><fig position="float" id="F3"><label>Figure 3</label><caption><p>Original risk group predicts benefit from PA-TACE. Kaplan&#x02013;Meier estimates illustrating differences in RFS and OS among low (A, B), intermediate (C, D), and high (E, F) risk group patients who underwent PA-TACE, compared to those who had hepatectomy alone. NR, not reach; OS, overall survival; PA-TACE, postoperative adjuvant transarterial chemoembolization; RFS, recurrence-free survival.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="js9-110-2556-g003" position="float"/></fig><p>Patients in the high-risk group exhibited significantly lower recurrence and higher survival rates after PA-TACE (Fig. <xref rid="F3" ref-type="fig">3</xref>E, F). The 5-year RFS rates were 44.9% (95% CI: 37.4&#x02013;53.9) and 30.8% (95% CI: 26.5&#x02013;35.8) for high-risk patients with PA-TACE or hepatectomy alone, respectively, demonstrating a PA-TACE absolute benefit of 14.1% in reducing of the risk of recurrence. Kaplan&#x02013;Meier curves showed significant differences between the low, intermediate, and high-risk subgroups (5-year RFS rates: 63.3, 44.7, and 38.2%, respectively, <italic toggle="yes">P</italic>&#x0003c;0.001, Fig. S6A, Supplemental Digital Content 1, <ext-link xlink:href="http://links.lww.com/JS9/B998" ext-link-type="uri">http://links.lww.com/JS9/B998</ext-link>; 10-year OS rates: 64.2, 61.7, and 45.6%, respectively, <italic toggle="yes">P</italic>&#x0003c;0.001, Fig. S6B, Supplemental Digital Content 1, <ext-link xlink:href="http://links.lww.com/JS9/B998" ext-link-type="uri">http://links.lww.com/JS9/B998</ext-link>).</p></sec><sec><title>HCC imaging and pathological classification (HIPC) prediction of PA-TACE benefit</title><p>For the interaction between IA and PA-TACE, we integrated IA into the original risk group for further stratification. The relative efficacy of PA-TACE versus hepatectomy alone did not differ in terms of RFS and OS in the low-risk group (Table <xref rid="T2" ref-type="table">2</xref>, Fig. S7A, B, Supplemental Digital Content 1, <ext-link xlink:href="http://links.lww.com/JS9/B998" ext-link-type="uri">http://links.lww.com/JS9/B998</ext-link>), in IA-negative patients in the intermediate risk group (subgroup1, Fig. S7C, D, Supplemental Digital Content 1, <ext-link xlink:href="http://links.lww.com/JS9/B998" ext-link-type="uri">http://links.lww.com/JS9/B998</ext-link>) and in patients in the high-risk group that were IA-negative or had a tumor diameter &#x02264;5&#x000a0;cm (subgroup2, Fig. S7E, F, Supplemental Digital Content 1, <ext-link xlink:href="http://links.lww.com/JS9/B998" ext-link-type="uri">http://links.lww.com/JS9/B998</ext-link>). IA-positive patients in the intermediate risk group (subgroup3) had no significant RFS benefit (Fig. S7G, Supplemental Digital Content 1, <ext-link xlink:href="http://links.lww.com/JS9/B998" ext-link-type="uri">http://links.lww.com/JS9/B998</ext-link>), but had significant OS benefit from PA-TACE (Fig. S7H, Supplemental Digital Content 1, <ext-link xlink:href="http://links.lww.com/JS9/B998" ext-link-type="uri">http://links.lww.com/JS9/B998</ext-link>). The addition of PA-TACE to hepatectomy alone achieved both RFS and OS (Fig. S7I, J, Supplemental Digital Content 1, <ext-link xlink:href="http://links.lww.com/JS9/B998" ext-link-type="uri">http://links.lww.com/JS9/B998</ext-link>) improvements in patients in the high-risk group who were IA-positive, and diameter &#x0003e;5&#x000a0;cm or patients with two or three tumors (subgroup4).</p><p>By integrating CT imaging and pathological factors, we developed the HIPC scheme, which categorized HCC patients after hepatectomy into three groups: HIPC1 (low-risk group), HIPC2 (subgroup1 and subgroup2), HIPC3 (subgroup3 and subgroup4), as illustrated by the Sankey diagram in Figure <xref rid="F4" ref-type="fig">4</xref>A. The absolute benefits in 5-year RFS and 10-year OS rates in the overall cohort, original risk group, and HIPC scheme are shown in Figure <xref rid="F4" ref-type="fig">4</xref>B.</p><fig position="float" id="F4"><label>Figure 4</label><caption><p>Sankey diagram and the absolute benefit of HIPC scheme. Sankey diagram illustrating the HIPC scheme (A) and the absolute benefit for improvements in the 5-year RFS and 10-year OS rates (B). HIPC, HCC imaging, and pathological classification. IA, internal arteries; OS, overall survival; RFS, recurrence-free survival.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="js9-110-2556-g004" position="float"/></fig><p>The HIPC scheme exhibited remarkable efficacy in discriminating between patients with and without PA-TACE benefit (Table <xref rid="T2" ref-type="table">2</xref>, Fig. <xref rid="F5" ref-type="fig">5</xref>). HIPC1 (HR, 0.872, 95% CI: 0.622&#x02013;1.222, <italic toggle="yes">P</italic>=0.425, Fig. <xref rid="F5" ref-type="fig">5</xref>A) and HIPC2 (HR, 0.989, 95% CI: 0.704&#x02013;1.390, <italic toggle="yes">P</italic>=0.949, Fig. <xref rid="F5" ref-type="fig">5</xref>B) patients obtained no significant RFS benefit from PA-TACE. In contrast, the addition of PA-TACE significantly improved RFS (HR, 0.636, 95% CI: 0.510&#x02013;0.793, <italic toggle="yes">P</italic>&#x0003c;0.001, Fig. <xref rid="F5" ref-type="fig">5</xref>C, D) in HIPC3 patients. Similar findings were observed in terms of OS (Fig. <xref rid="F5" ref-type="fig">5</xref>E-H). Furthermore, a test for an interaction between the HIPC group and PA-TACE indicated that benefit from PA-TACE was superior among patients in the HIPC3 group than among those in HIPC1 and HIPC2 groups in terms of RFS (<italic toggle="yes">P</italic>=0.096) and OS (<italic toggle="yes">P</italic>=0.013). Examples of without and with PA-TACE in HIPC3 are shown in Figure S8&#x02013;S11 (Supplemental Digital Content 1, <ext-link xlink:href="http://links.lww.com/JS9/B998" ext-link-type="uri">http://links.lww.com/JS9/B998</ext-link>). The 5-year recurrence risk was 57.7% (48.6&#x02013;65.2%) and 73.0% (68.0&#x02013;77.2%) for HIPC3 patients treated with and without PA-TACE, respectively, demonstrating a PA-TACE absolute benefit of 15.3% in reducing the risk of recurrence. The 10-year OS rates were 53.8% (95% CI: 44.4&#x02013;65.2) and 37.2% (95% CI: 31.7&#x02013;43.6) for patients who underwent PA-TACE or hepatectomy alone, respectively, exhibiting a PA-TACE absolute benefit of 16.6% in reducing of the risk of death.</p><fig position="float" id="F5"><label>Figure 5</label><caption><p>HIPC, a new stratification scheme based on imaging and pathological indicators, predicts RFS and OS benefits from PA-TACE. RFS (A&#x02013;D) and OS (E&#x02013;H) improvement for PA-TACE versus hepatectomy alone in HIPC1, HIPC2, and HIPC3 group patients. The forest plot illustrates RFS (D) and OS (H) improvements for PA-TACE versus hepatectomy alone across HIPC1, HIPC2, and HIPC3 group patients. HIPC, HCC imaging and pathological classification; NR, not reach; OS, overall survival; PA-TACE, postoperative adjuvant transarterial chemoembolization; RFS, recurrence-free survival.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="js9-110-2556-g005" position="float"/></fig></sec><sec><title>HIPC is a robust scheme for the prediction of PA-TACE benefits in HCC</title><p>The difference in benefit between the HIPC groups was robust in most clinical (Fig. S12, S13, Supplemental Digital Content 1, <ext-link xlink:href="http://links.lww.com/JS9/B998" ext-link-type="uri">http://links.lww.com/JS9/B998</ext-link>) and surgical factor subgroups (Fig. S14, S15, Supplemental Digital Content 1, <ext-link xlink:href="http://links.lww.com/JS9/B998" ext-link-type="uri">http://links.lww.com/JS9/B998</ext-link>). Patients in the HIPC3 group obtained significant RFS and OS benefits from PA-TACE in both univariate and multivariate analyses (all <italic toggle="yes">P</italic>&#x0003c;0.001), while patients in the HIPC1 and HIPC2 groups did not obtain significant RFS or OS benefits in both univariate and multivariate analyses (Table S6, Supplemental Digital Content 1, <ext-link xlink:href="http://links.lww.com/JS9/B998" ext-link-type="uri">http://links.lww.com/JS9/B998</ext-link>). At the same time, the Kaplan&#x02013;Meier curves showed significant differences between the three HIPC subgroups (5-year RFS rates: 63.7, 49.8, and 34.8%, respectively, <italic toggle="yes">P</italic>&#x0003c;0.001; 10-year OS rates: 64.6, 60.0, and 45.4%, respectively, <italic toggle="yes">P</italic>&#x0003c;0.001, Fig. S16, Supplemental Digital Content 1, <ext-link xlink:href="http://links.lww.com/JS9/B998" ext-link-type="uri">http://links.lww.com/JS9/B998</ext-link>), indicating HIPC3 group was at high-risk of recurrence.</p><p>
Figure <xref rid="F6" ref-type="fig">6</xref> illustrates the updated version of the suggestion for PA-TACE according to the results of our study. Our HIPC scheme may decrease the number of patients undergoing TACE by ~36.5% (Fig. <xref rid="F4" ref-type="fig">4</xref>A).</p><fig position="float" id="F6"><label>Figure 6</label><caption><p>Flowchart showing the proposed HIPC scheme for PA-TACE suggestion. The figure is based on the original risk stratification and has been modified by adding IA and tumor diameter, and the PA-TACE suggestion has been given based on our results and absolute survival benefit. HIPC, HCC imaging and pathological classification; IA, internal arteries; OS, overall survival; PA-TACE, postoperative adjuvant transarterial chemoembolization; RFS, recurrence-free survival.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="js9-110-2556-g006" position="float"/></fig></sec><sec sec-type="subjects"><title>Tumor characteristics of HIPC3 patients</title><p>HIPC3 patients had high tumor diameter, Edmondson&#x02013;Steiner grade, AFP, TTPVI, necrosis, nonsmooth margin, and less halo and capsule compared with HIPC1 and HIPC2 patients (Table <xref rid="T3" ref-type="table">3</xref>). Using 2 years as the threshold, early recurrence was observed in 22.3% HIPC1 (<italic toggle="yes">n</italic>=127), 36.7% HIPC2 (<italic toggle="yes">n</italic>=121), and 55.8% HIPC3 (<italic toggle="yes">n</italic>=328) patients. For HIPC1 and HIPC2 patients, early recurrence rates between the groups were similar. Interestingly, we found that the early recurrence rate of the PA-TACE group was significantly lower than that in the hepatectomy alone group in HIPC3 patients, whereas the late recurrence rates between these groups were similar (Table S7, Supplemental Digital Content 1, <ext-link xlink:href="http://links.lww.com/JS9/B998" ext-link-type="uri">http://links.lww.com/JS9/B998</ext-link>). Moreover, the extrahepatic recurrence rate in the PA-TACE group (12/49) was significantly higher than that in the hepatectomy alone group (22/186; <italic toggle="yes">P</italic>=0.025) in HIPC1 patients, while were similar in HIPC2 and HIPC3 patients.</p><table-wrap position="float" id="T3"><label>Table 3</label><caption><p>Baseline clinical characteristics of patients in different HIPC groups.</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><col align="left" width="1*" span="1"/><col align="left" width="1*" span="1"/><col align="left" width="1*" span="1"/><col align="left" width="1*" span="1"/><col align="left" width="1*" span="1"/><thead><tr><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1" axis="1">Variable</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1" axis="1">HIPC1 (<italic toggle="yes">n</italic>=570)</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1" axis="1">HIPC2 (<italic toggle="yes">n</italic>=330)</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1" axis="1">HIPC3 (<italic toggle="yes">n</italic>=588)</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1" axis="1">
<italic toggle="yes">P</italic>
</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Age (years)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">54 (46&#x02013;62)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">53 (45&#x02013;61)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">51 (43&#x02013;61)</td><td align="char" char="." rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.001</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Sex</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="char" char="." rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.19</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;Female</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">79 (13.9%)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">33 (10.0%)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">67 (11.4%)</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;Male</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">491 (86.1%)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">297 (90.0%)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">521 (88.6%)</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">MVI</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="char" char="." rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x0003c;0.001</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;Negative</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">570 (100.0%)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">120 (36.4%)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">252 (42.9%)</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;Positive</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0 (0.0%)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">210 (63.6%)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">336 (57.1%)</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Diameter (cm, IQR)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">3.0 (2.2&#x02013;3.9)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">4.4 (2.9&#x02013;5.6)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">7.9 (6.2&#x02013;10.2)</td><td align="char" char="." rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x0003c;0.001</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Edmondson&#x02013;Steiner</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="char" char="." rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x0003c;0.001</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;I&#x02013;II</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">414 (72.6%)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">195 (59.1%)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">324 (55.1%)</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;III&#x02013;IV</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">156 (27.4%)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">135 (40.9%)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">264 (44.9%)</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Etiology</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="char" char="." rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.53</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;HBV/HCV</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">518 (90.9%)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">293 (88.8%)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">525 (89.3%)</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;Other disease origins</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">52 (9.1%)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">37 (11.2%)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">63 (10.7%)</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">ALT (U/l)</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="char" char="." rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x0003c;0.001</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;&#x02264;40</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">381 (66.8%)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">202 (61.2%)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">311 (52.9%)</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;&#x0003e;40</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">189 (33.2%)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">128 (38.8%)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">277 (47.1%)</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">ALB (g/l)</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="char" char="." rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.049</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;&#x02264;35</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">50 (8.8%)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">19 (5.8%)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">62 (10.5%)</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;&#x0003e;35</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">520 (91.2%)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">311 (94.2%)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">526 (89.5%)</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">AST (U/l)</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="char" char="." rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x0003c;0.001</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;&#x02264;40</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">415 (72.8%)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">237 (71.8%)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">286 (48.6%)</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;&#x0003e;40</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">155 (27.2%)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">93 (28.2%)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">302 (51.4%)</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">GGT (U/l)</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="char" char="." rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x0003c;0.001</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;&#x02264;75</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">416 (73.0%)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">227 (68.8%)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">295 (50.2%)</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;&#x0003e;75</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">154 (27.0%)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">103 (31.2%)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">293 (49.8%)</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">TBIL (&#x003bc;mol/l)</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="char" char="." rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.025</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;&#x02264;17.1</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">439 (77.0%)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">227 (68.8%)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">435 (74.0%)</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;&#x0003e;17.1</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">131 (23.0%)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">103 (31.2%)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">153 (26.0%)</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">AFP (ng/ml)</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="char" char="." rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x0003c;0.001</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;&#x02264;200</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">436 (76.5%)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">222 (67.3%)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">325 (55.3%)</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;&#x0003e;200</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">134 (23.5%)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">108 (32.7%)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">263 (44.7%)</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Necrosis</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="char" char="." rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x0003c;0.001</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;Positive</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">132 (23.2%)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">149 (45.2%)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">506 (86.1%)</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;Negative</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">438 (76.8%)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">181 (54.8%)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">82 (13.9%)</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Halo</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="char" char="." rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x0003c;0.001</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;Positive</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">154 (27.0%)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">56 (17.0%)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">78 (13.3%)</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;Negative</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">416 (73.0%)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">274 (83.0%)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">510 (86.7%)</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Capsule</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="char" char="." rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x0003c;0.001</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;Positive</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">232 (40.7%)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">89 (27.0%)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">90 (15.3%)</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;Negative</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">338 (59.3%)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">241 (73.0%)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">498 (84.7%)</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Margin</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="char" char="." rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x0003c;0.001</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;Smooth</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">453 (79.5%)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">196 (59.4%)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">252 (42.9%)</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;Nonsmooth</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">117 (20.5%)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">134 (40.6%)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">336 (57.1%)</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">TTPVI</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="char" char="." rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x0003c;0.001</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;Positive</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">93 (16.3%)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">78 (23.6%)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">434 (73.8%)</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;Negative</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">477 (83.7%)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">252 (76.4%)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">154 (26.2%)</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">AJCC</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="char" char="." rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x0003c;0.001</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;Stage I</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">570 (100.0%)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">137 (41.5%)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">209 (35.5%)</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;Stage II/IIIA</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0 (0.0%)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">193 (58.5%)</td><td align="char" char="(" rowspan="1" colspan="1">379 (64.5%)</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><fn fn-type="other"><p>AFP, alpha-fetoprotein; AJCC, American Joint Committee on Cancer; ALB, albumin; ALT, alanine aminotransferase; AST, aspartate aminotransferase; GGT, gamma-glutamyl transpeptidase; HBV, hepatitis B virus; HCV, hepatitis C virus; HIPC, HCC imaging and pathological classification; MVI, microvascular invasion; TBIL, total bilirubin; TTPVI, two-trait predictor of venous invasion.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></sec></sec><sec sec-type="discussion"><title>Discussion</title><p>The heterogeneous nature of HCC requires highly individualized patient selection. To date, no individualized, CT-based assessment for predicting benefit from PA-TACE has been reported. This study confirmed that IA predicted a benefit from PA-TACE, with IA-positive patients selectively obtaining a significant benefit from PA-TACE versus hepatectomy alone. By comprehensively incorporating CT imaging (tumor diameter, tumor number, and IA) and pathological (MVI) features, we developed the HIPC scheme for optimizing PA-TACE decision-making. Our analysis showed that PA-TACE was associated with longer OS and RFS improvements in HIPC3 patients, whereas survival outcomes in HIPC1 and HIPC2 patients did not differ between the PA-TACE and hepatectomy alone groups.</p><p>The use of IA as a predictive biomarker has several advantages: CT or MRI is routinely performed preoperatively; IA can be easily recognized by distinguishing discrete arteries within the tumor and the interobserver agreement is good or excellent<sup><xref rid="R32" ref-type="bibr">32</xref>,<xref rid="R33" ref-type="bibr">33</xref></sup>; IA is a prevalent feature presented in 28.9&#x02013;52.3% of HCC<sup><xref rid="R32" ref-type="bibr">32</xref>,<xref rid="R34" ref-type="bibr">34</xref>,<xref rid="R35" ref-type="bibr">35</xref></sup>. Thus, a large proportion of HCC patients may benefit from using IA as a selection criterion. MVI has been reported as an important indicator predicting benefit from PA-TACE in HCC after hepatectomy<sup><xref rid="R5" ref-type="bibr">5</xref>&#x02013;<xref rid="R7" ref-type="bibr">7</xref>,<xref rid="R10" ref-type="bibr">10</xref>,<xref rid="R14" ref-type="bibr">14</xref>,<xref rid="R36" ref-type="bibr">36</xref>&#x02013;<xref rid="R39" ref-type="bibr">39</xref></sup>. Studies have also reported IA as a high-risk recurrence indicator and a potential of predictor of MVI (OR=5.683, 95% CI: 4.222&#x02013;7.651, <italic toggle="yes">P</italic>&#x0003c;0.001), RFS (HR, 2.041, 95% CI: 1.721&#x02013;2.421, <italic toggle="yes">P</italic>&#x0003c;0.001), and OS (HR, 2.540, 95% CI: 1.932&#x02013;3.340, <italic toggle="yes">P</italic>&#x0003c;0.001) after HCC resection, which is an important feature of TTPVI derived from a venous invasion gene profile associated with angiogenesis, cellular proliferation, and matrix invasion<sup><xref rid="R18" ref-type="bibr">18</xref>,<xref rid="R24" ref-type="bibr">24</xref></sup>. Meanwhile, IA has been identified as a significant predictor of a good response to TACE was demonstrated in previous studies<sup><xref rid="R40" ref-type="bibr">40</xref></sup>. In our study, IA interacted with PA-TACE in terms of RFS and OS. Therefore, IA may be a complementary biomarker to traditional clinical indices of PA-TACE response in HCC.</p><p>Performing PA-TACE to reduce the risk of recurrence and prolong survival is an important decision for patients diagnosed with very early-stage to intermediate-stage HCC receiving hepatectomy. However, official PA-TACE recommendation guidelines differ, possibly because of different etiologies<sup><xref rid="R2" ref-type="bibr">2</xref>&#x02013;<xref rid="R4" ref-type="bibr">4</xref>,<xref rid="R41" ref-type="bibr">41</xref>,<xref rid="R42" ref-type="bibr">42</xref></sup>. Our HIPC scheme demonstrated significant potential in guiding clinical decisions regarding the addition of PA-TACE to hepatectomy in early to intermediate-stage HCC, and encourages future investigations on novel imaging features for clinical decisions. Our analysis showed that HIPC3 patients benefited from PA-TACE in terms of RFS and OS, whereas HIPC1 and HIPC2 patients did not. Moreover, our scheme showed a similar trend in most subgroups and also in two different centers. In the HIPC3 group, the Kaplan&#x02013;Meier curve of the PA-TACE arm tended to plateau after 36 months, suggesting that a substantial proportion of patients may achieve long-term survival benefits after PA-TACE. However, TACE may accelerate the loss of liver function, suppress antitumor immunity and promote the development of hepatic cirrhosis<sup><xref rid="R9" ref-type="bibr">9</xref>,<xref rid="R41" ref-type="bibr">41</xref></sup>. The HIPC scheme may prevent ~36.5% of patients from undergoing PA-TACE, avoiding such adverse side-effects. TTPVI also interacted with PA-TACE in terms of OS (<italic toggle="yes">P</italic>=0.035). Therefore, in our HIPC scheme, HIPC3 patients had a higher proportion of TTPVI than HIPC1 and HIPC2 patients, demonstrating the rationality of the HIPC scheme.</p><p>Interestingly, our results indicated that the therapeutic effect of PA-TACE in HIPC3 patients primarily relied on a reduction in early postoperative recurrence, similar to previous studies using MVI, original risk group, circulating tumor cells, COCH, and RMP<sup><xref rid="R5" ref-type="bibr">5</xref>,<xref rid="R6" ref-type="bibr">6</xref>,<xref rid="R14" ref-type="bibr">14</xref>&#x02013;<xref rid="R16" ref-type="bibr">16</xref></sup>. PA-TACE may improve the prognosis of HCC patients with high-recurrence risk by treating a minimal residual disease or occult intrahepatic lesions that imaging fails to detect before hepatectomy<sup><xref rid="R43" ref-type="bibr">43</xref></sup>. In our study, the HIPC3 group who would benefit from PA-TACE was a high-recurrence risk patient, which was similar to previous studies<sup><xref rid="R5" ref-type="bibr">5</xref>,<xref rid="R6" ref-type="bibr">6</xref>,<xref rid="R14" ref-type="bibr">14</xref></sup>. Nonetheless, additional postoperative adjuvant therapies are required to reduce late recurrence rates, thereby improving patient prognosis.</p><p>Our study had several limitations that should be acknowledged. First, its retrospective nature was a potential source of selection bias, but we intended to minimize such limitation by inverse probability of treatment weighting. Second, our cohort mostly included HBV positive patients; therefore, it may not be representative of patients with other etiologies. Third, patients receiving other postoperative adjuvant therapies, such as nucleoside analogs, hepatic arterial infusion chemotherapy, sorafenib therapy and immunotherapy, were not assessed. In the future, prospective, multicenter, large population studies are needed to validate the value of the HIPC scheme as a biomarker for guiding PA-TACE. Also, investigating whether the HIPC scheme could be extended to hepatic arterial infusion chemotherapy, sorafenib, and immunotherapy is worthwhile. Moreover, exploring other postoperative adjuvant therapies to reduce recurrence rates and prolong survival in patients who cannot benefit from PA-TACE is essential.</p><p>This study demonstrated a greater value provision on CT imaging and prediction of significant PA-TACE benefit based on tumor diameter, tumor number, MVI, and IA in HCC patients treated with hepatectomy. The proposed HIPC scheme comprehensively integrates these indicators to stratify patients with and without survival benefits from PA-TACE. As a preoperative CT imaging tool that measures preferential response and degree of benefit, the HIPC scheme may help individualize patient selection for PA-TACE.</p></sec><sec><title>Ethical approval</title><p>The study was approved by the Institutional Ethics Review Board of the two medical centers. The approval number was 2019-KY-021-01. The requirement for informed consent was waived (retrospective analysis of CT images) by the Institutional Ethics Review Board of the two medical centers.</p></sec><sec><title>Consent</title><p>The requirement for informed consent was waived for its retrospective nature.</p></sec><sec><title>Sources of funding</title><p>This work was funded by the National Key R&#x00026;D Program of China (2021YFF1201003), National Science Foundation for Young Scientists of China (82302315), Natural Science Foundation of China (82370674), Guangdong Basic and Applied Basic Research Foundation (2023A1515012242 and 2021A1515011305), Guangdong Provincial Key Laboratory of Artificial Intelligence in Medical Image Analysis and Application (2022B1212010011), and President Foundation of Zhujiang Hospital, Southern Medical University (yzjj2021qn23). The funders had no role in study design, data collection, data analysis, interpretation, writing of the report, and the decision of submitting it for publication.</p></sec><sec><title>Author contribution</title><p>X.L., C.L., Z.L., and X.Q.: conceptualization; X.L., X.L., Z.L., J.L., Z.Q., Z.G., and L.Z.: data curation, formal analysis, methodology, resources, and software; X.L., C.L., Z.L., X.Q., X.L., and Z.L.: drafting of the manuscript; X.L., C.L., Z.L., X.Q., X.L., Z.L., and W.L.: validation and visualization; C.L., Z.L., X.Q., and X.L.: writing &#x02013; original draft and writing &#x02013; review and editing; C.L. and Z.L.: supervision. All authors read and approved the final manuscript.</p></sec><sec sec-type="COI-statement"><title>Conflicts of interest disclosure</title><p>The authors have declared that no competing interest exists.</p></sec><sec><title>Research registration unique identifying number (UIN)</title><p>
